== 1 left join, predicate in ON (partial unique index)
                   QUERY PLAN                    
-------------------------------------------------
 Hash Left Join
   Hash Cond: (a.k = b.k)
   ->  Seq Scan on t a
   ->  Hash
         ->  Index Only Scan using t_k_s1 on t b
(5 rows)

== 2 left join, predicate in a subquery (partial unique index)
                  QUERY PLAN                   
-----------------------------------------------
 Hash Left Join
   Hash Cond: (a.k = t.k)
   ->  Seq Scan on t a
   ->  Hash
         ->  Index Only Scan using t_k_s1 on t
(5 rows)

== 3 DISTINCT over the key within the scope (partial unique index)
               QUERY PLAN                
-----------------------------------------
 Unique
   ->  Index Only Scan using t_k_s1 on t
(2 rows)

== 4 inner self-join on the key within the scope (self-join elimination, PG 18)
 enable_self_join_elimination 
------------------------------
 on
(1 row)

              QUERY PLAN              
--------------------------------------
 Merge Join
   Merge Cond: (a.k = b.k)
   ->  Index Scan using t_k_s1 on t a
   ->  Index Scan using t_k_s1 on t b
(4 rows)

== control: the same queries with a full unique index
== 5 left join (full unique index)
   QUERY PLAN    
-----------------
 Seq Scan on u a
(1 row)

== 6 left join, predicate in a subquery (full unique index)
   QUERY PLAN    
-----------------
 Seq Scan on u a
(1 row)

== 7 DISTINCT (full unique index)
       QUERY PLAN        
-------------------------
 HashAggregate
   Group Key: k
   ->  Seq Scan on u
         Filter: (s = 1)
(4 rows)

== 8 inner self-join (full unique index)
               QUERY PLAN                
-----------------------------------------
 Seq Scan on u b
   Filter: ((k IS NOT NULL) AND (s = 1))
(2 rows)

